UID:curiodyssey-10000827@local-events
DESCRIPTION:@ 			\n			\n							\n		\n			\n\n\n\n\nBundle up and discover w
 ho’s spending the winter in the baylands right outside our doors. Join C
 uriOdyssey educators for a guided hike through Coyote Point’s wetlands\,
  where we’ll look and listen for resident and migratory birds and count 
 the feathered visitors that call our shoreline home this season. No birdin
 g experience needed!\n\nThis event is free and open to the public. RSVP is
  required. All children must be accompanied by their grown-up for the dura
 tion of the hike.\n\nWe will gather at CuriOdyssey before heading out to t
 he marsh together. Participants of all ages are welcome. More information
 \, including the exact meeting location and what to bring\, will be shared
  upon registration.\n\nPlease note that parking is managed by San Mateo Co
 unty Parks\, and…\n\nAges: Family / kids\nSource: https://curiodyssey.or
 g/event/winter-bird-count-hike/2026-12-18/\nLast synced: 2026-11-26 14:08 
